WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
ReconcileHub. Monthly access-roster reconciliation that never merges two people on a guess.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.067
1. This month's inputs: access-system roster, last month's approvals, new registrations. Three inputs: the door-access system's roster, last month's approvals, new registrations, with the usual mess planted.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:30.800
2. Reconcile: exact matches decided, everything else held. Exact id matches are decided automatically. An id change, a row with no id and a likely duplicate registration are held with a suggestion.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.867
3. Try to approve before review. Approval is refused while cases are held, and a note to the space admins is drafted.

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:49.533
4. A reviewer decides the held cases. A reviewer records same-person for each. Only now do they become rename and fix-id actions.

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:55.667
5. Approve. Approved: a hashed roster snapshot, an import workbook and a change report.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:01:01.133
6. Run it again: same inputs, same decisions. Same inputs and decisions again: identical hash, nothing new written.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:11.533
7. A late registration arrives after approval. A late registration after approval is refused unless superseded with a reason; v2 sits beside v1.

00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:18.067
What it produced: Access_import_2026-11_v1.xlsx - Import tab. The import workbook: one row per action, with the reason.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:24.600
What it produced: exports/2026-11/Change_report_2026-11_v1.md. The change report, reviewed cases included.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:31.133
What it produced: outbox/2026-11/2026-11-held-cases.eml. The draft to space admins while cases were held.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:38.133
What this run showed: Ids normalised, originals kept; Near-matches suggested, never merged; Approval blocked until people decided; Re-runs idempotent; changes need a reason. Tests: 15 passed.
